              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for the petrol pump, then the German for the oil change."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: anspringen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "anspringen — \"to start (of an engine)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Im Winter springt unser Auto morgens schlecht an. In winter our car is hard to start in the mornings."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Separable; Perfekt with sein: der Motor ist nicht angesprungen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "anspringen is built from an 'on' and springen 'to jump', inherited from Proto-Germanic springaną (EtymDB): an engine that jumps into life. English spring is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
