          "title": "You'll want to know: die Batterie",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Batterie — \"the battery\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Die Batterie ist leer, weil das Licht die ganze Nacht an war. The battery is flat because the light was on all night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Batterien. The battery in a phone is usually der Akku."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Batterie was borrowed from French batterie, first 'a beating', then a row of guns, from battre 'to beat' (EtymDB), which goes back to Latin battuere 'to beat' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
